  "candidates": [
    {
      "id": "REVIEW-AUTORESOLVE-AUTHORED-SHIELD-PROJECTION-001",
      "severity": "P2 conditional: authored threat protection does not consistently reach shield defense",
      "classification": "New bounded 95e producer-to-consumer trace; historical aliases and design policy remain open.",
      "trace": "The checked-in town_watch profile says protection=shielded; the catalog validator admits that spelling and bestiary conversion produces Protection::Shielded. authored_threat_combatant starts from Combatant::new and default equipment, builds the melee weapon and grants trained block skill for Shielded or Armored. Only the Armored branch sets shield_block_bonus=1.0; neither branch assigns shield_side or defense_item_id. Thus the selected shielded profile retains bonus 0 and side None despite its authored protection tag. Its melee weapon may still support an ordinary block: this is not a claim that it cannot defend. For a separately selected Armored profile the producer sets a positive shield bonus but retains side None. A selected block then reaches shield_aligned_response, whose None-side branch returns the input response unchanged instead of applying the directional shield geometry; the positive bonus is also consumed by melee-defense and combat-power calculations. The normal authored iteration equipment example assigns bonus, hand and defense item together, demonstrating a different selected producer, not universal admission.",
      "safeguards_and_limits": "The public builder can be called with the checked-in threat ID, and selected strategic encounter/mission and observer-power paths call the same builder. Incident source names town_watch and armed_retainer but its complete battle handoff and a realized encounter were not traced. The code does not prove that every armored threat is intended to have a shield, which hand or item it should use, that a block is selected in a particular battle, or that the player observed a discrepancy. No tactical-session parity or database persistence is inferred. Different complete producers, catalog semantics, output visibility and historical aliases remain open.",
      "connected_repair": "Reconcile the authored protection contract and its representation with the actual combat equipment projection, shield presence, hand, item identity, block selection, directional alignment and observer-power calculation. If armor and shield are independent properties, represent the supported combinations explicitly; do not infer shield possession for all armored threats or suppress ordinary weapon defense. Keep player-relevant defense factors legible and preserve the strategic/tactical authority boundary.",
      "acceptance": "After separate implementation authorization, verify each supported shielded, armored-only, shield-plus-armor and unshielded profile under the chosen authoring contract, including actual hand/geometry, item identity where present, ordinary weapon block and observer-power consistency. Product validation remains deferred.",
      "discovery": "partial; authored shield/armor policy, actual selected encounters, all consumers and historical aliases open",
      "repair": "not started",
      "validation": "not performed"
    }
  ],
